Package: geokmeans
Type: Package
Title: Fast and Eco-Friendly k-Means Clustering Algorithms
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Parichit", "Sharma", email = "parishar@iu.edu",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph")),
    person("Hasan", "Kurban", role = "aut"))
Description: R package for fast C++ implementations of several k-means clustering algorithms
    under a uniform interface, including Lloyd's algorithm, Elkan, Hamerly,
    Annulus, Exponion, Ball k-means, and the bound-free Geometric-k-means
    method of Sharma et al. (2025) <doi:10.1007/s10994-025-06891-1>.
    Geometric-k-means treats data points as first-class citizens to channel
    computation toward high-expressive points, reducing distance computations,
    memory use, and runtime while preserving cluster quality. The algorithms
    are exposed to R via 'Rcpp' and 'RcppEigen' and return the final centroids,
    optional per-point cluster assignments, and computational statistics.
